  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Toria's friend holds a barrel of $150$ marbles in front of her, each with a slightly different size or color.  If she reaches in and grabs five of them, how many different groups of five marbles can Toria select?",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $150$ marbles, so $n=150.$ We want to select $5$ of those marbles from the bag, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different potential groups of five marbles is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{150}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{150!}{(150-5)!\\,5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{150!}{145!5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{150\\cdot 149\\cdot 148\\cdot 147\\cdot 146\\cdot \\cancel{145!}}{\\cancel{145!}5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{150\\cdot 149\\cdot 148\\cdot 147\\cdot 146}{5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =591\\,600\\,030.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
